  "prompt_text": "The figure summarizes a feed-forward immune circuit centered on BAFF, B cells, and T follicular helper (T_FH) cells that appears to promote autoantibody production. A plasmablast at the left is shown releasing autoantibodies and expressing several BAFF receptors, including BAFF-R, BCMA, and TACI, suggesting that BAFF can directly support antibody-secreting cells. Naive and memory B cells below are also linked upward toward the plasmablast stage, indicating progression of B-cell activation and differentiation.\n\nOn the right, a T_FH cell expresses BAFF-R and is connected to the plasmablast by a large loop labeled with IL-21 across the top and IL-6 across the bottom. This implies reciprocal signaling: T_FH-derived IL-21 supports plasmablast responses, while IL-6 contributes to T_FH-cell help or maintenance. BAFF itself is placed between the two cell types with arrows pointing toward the plasmablast and from the T_FH side, highlighting BAFF as a shared survival or activation factor.\n\nA dendritic cell at the bottom appears to be an upstream source of BAFF that influences both B cells and T_FH cells. Overall, the image depicts an interconnected inflammatory network that reinforces B-cell survival, plasmablast generation, and pathogenic autoantibody production.",
